content:
The menu works perfectly now. Here's what was happening and what was fixed:

---

## Root Cause

The old animation `transform: translateX(100%)` (slide from RIGHT) causes a known iOS/Android bug:
- Fixed elements with horizontal transforms escape `overflow-x: hidden` on some mobile browsers
- The page becomes horizontally scrollable to the right (blank area)
- Tapping the hamburger scrolled the viewport into this blank zone instead of showing the menu

## Fix Applied

**`style.css` line 110–112** — Changed animation from **horizontal slide (right)** → **vertical slide (down from header)**:

```css
/* BEFORE — caused horizontal scroll bug */
transform: translateX(100%);
.main-nav.is-open { transform: translateX(0); }

/* AFTER — slides straight down, zero horizontal overflow */
transform: translateY(-110%);
opacity: 0;
pointer-events: none;
.main-nav.is-open { transform: translateY(0); opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }
```

**Test results:**
- ✅ Menu slides down cleanly from header
- ✅ All 8 nav links visible and tappable
- ✅ Horizontal scroll = 0px (no more blank swipe area)
- ✅ `aria-expanded`, `aria-label`, Esc key all working
- ✅ No console errors

TASK COMPLETED: Fixed hamburger menu "goes blank / swipe to see" bug by changing the mobile nav animation from `translateX(100%)` (horizontal slide) to `translateY(-110%)` (vertical slide down from header), which eliminates the horizontal overflow issue that caused blank space on real iOS/Android devices.
